& [Fold_1_Identity] makes the boundary unmistakable
  + binary name is cantor-procedure-experiment
  + response profile is cantor-procedure-tool-cli/0.1
  + this is an adapter over CPPE-I08, not a new semantic engine
  + existing cantor and cantor-mcp meanings remain unchanged

& [Fold_2_Inputs] closes ingress
  + schema takes no input payload
  + run accepts one strict RunRequest containing exact ProviderNeutralToolSchema, ToolCallProposal, and AuthorshipLaneEvidence
  + verify accepts one strict VerifyRequest containing the run inputs plus FakeControllerOutcome
  + run and verify read from one optional --input path or otherwise stdin
  + input is nonempty and bounded to 16 MiB
  + unknown commands, flags, fields, duplicate flags, missing paths, malformed JSON, and excess bytes are typed invalid input

& [Fold_3_Processing] preserves deterministic semantics
  + schema calls provider_neutral_exchange_schema
  + run calls run_fake_controller_exchange then verify_fake_controller_outcome on the returned value
  + verify calls verify_fake_controller_outcome without producing a replacement outcome
  + no fallback, coercion, digest repair, identity minting, or inferred authority occurs

& [Fold_4_Outputs] supports tool controllers
  + stdout contains exactly one newline-terminated JSON response
  + stderr contains diagnostics only
  + success schema returns the exact closed schema
  + success run returns the exact independently verified outcome
  + success verify returns a positive verification record bound to schema, call, result, and transcript digests
  + faults contain bounded code, stage, and message
  + all responses repeat experiment grade and zero-provider zero-external-effect residuals

& [Fold_5_ExitSemantics] are stable
  + 0 means schema produced, completed run verified, or supplied outcome verified
  + 2 means invalid command, arguments, input transport, or JSON
  + 3 means the controller produced a valid refused outcome
  + 4 means generated or supplied outcome verification failed
  + 5 means internal construction or serialization failed

& [Fold_6_TrustAndSecurity] refuses semantic promotion
  + strict serde denies unknown fields
  + caller supplies every identity and digest
  + existing core replay is authority for validation
  + file input is read-only and never interpreted as trusted merely because it was readable
  + no secrets, signatures, keys, environment variables, network addresses, or ambient authority are accepted
  + refusal is preserved as refusal and never rewritten as success

& [Fold_7_ProofAndLifecycle] keeps the adapter honest
  + real subprocess tests cover schema, stdin run, file run, refusal, verify, tamper, malformed JSON, unknown fields, size limit, and deterministic replay
  + direct core outcome equals decoded CLI outcome
  + formatting, lint, workspace tests, and release overflow tests remain required
  + completion review records that live provider count, production count, and external-effect count remain zero
  + rollback removes one binary source, one Cargo binary stanza, tests, and governance without changing core semantics

& [PrunedGrowth] keeps future work separate
  + future provider controllers may consume this wire profile only after separate SJS
  + future MCP projection may reuse the same request and response meanings only after separate SJS
  + future textual source, service, persistence, multi-participant junction, model execution, and FPGA paths are not latent permissions
